  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Architecture & Testing Discipline. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 24: David Heinemeier Hansson (DHH) from RailsConf 2014 (2014).",
  "RailsConf 2014 in Chicago was the epicenter of the debate between pragmatic product velocity and strict architectural dogma, debated in corridors with Martin Fowler and Uncle Bob.",
  "What inspired DHH's literary conception of software as writing? What sparked his 'TDD is Dead' keynote at the Chicago Sheraton? What principles guided David Heinemeier Hansson (DHH) when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: z94-DGthrfY). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Software architecture is not a math proof; it is prose meant for human understanding. Clarity and taste matter more than dogmatic ceremony. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "Thank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 25. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]